{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Then</b>, <b>in their sarbelim</b> — these are the upper garment, and it is the custom of the nations to burn people in their garments, though they are of no consequence at all." "<b>And their karbelatahon</b> — like \"and David was wrapped (מכרבל) in a linen robe\"." "<b>And their pateshehon</b> — tunics or trousers." "<b>And their levushehon</b> — the rest of the garments."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:38.926246792Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}